## 📁 Dataset

The dataset used in this project is **very large**, so it is hosted on **Google Drive** instead of GitHub.

### 🔗 Download Dataset
👉 [Click here to download the dataset](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1rSkdHOjh1O82u4pFjhPRkM-UN8AtkeO7?usp=sharing)

---

## 📦 Dataset Structure

The dataset is organized into the following splits:

- **Train Dataset**  
  Used for training the deepfake detection model.

- **Validation Dataset**  
  Used for hyperparameter tuning and model selection.

- **Test Dataset**  
  Used for final evaluation and performance reporting.

Each split contains **real and synthetic (TTS-generated) audio samples**, resampled to **16 kHz**, following the experimental setup described in the paper.

---

## 📄 Original Dataset & Reference

This dataset is derived from the **TIMIT-TTS corpus**, which is a synthetic extension of the original TIMIT dataset.

**Original Paper:**
> *TIMIT-TTS: A Text-to-Speech Dataset for Multimodal Synthetic Media Detection*  
> Salvi et al., IEEE Access, 2023

The dataset includes speech generated by **multiple Text-to-Speech (TTS) models**, making it suitable for benchmarking **audio deepfake detection systems**.

📌 **Note:**  
This dataset contains **only synthetic and non-identifiable speech data** and is intended **strictly for research and academic use**.

---

## ⚠️ Important Notes

- Due to GitHub file size limitations, the dataset is **not included** in this repository.
- Please ensure you have sufficient storage and a stable internet connection before downloading.
- Follow the dataset license and citation requirements when using it in publications.

